The TypeScript adaptation keeps the previous sample as a JavaScript number per
channel, wraps int16_t and int32_t differences in two's complement, rounds float
differences with Math.fround and keeps double differences unrounded. It
implements no options: the timeline-internal enable path (which resets the
previous sample to silence) and runtime commands are refused before output. The
aintegral filter defined in the same file is not adapted. Non-finite floating
input is refused, because NaN payloads would not be reproduced.
